  <h1>Home Page</h1>
  <p>
    A URL shortener is a simple tool that turns a long web address into a short, clean link. When you click the short
    link, it quickly sends you to the original page. Popular tools like Bitly and TinyURL help make links easy to share.
  </p>

  <h3>Why People Use Short Links</h3>
  <p>
    Save space: Great for text messages or social media posts with character limits. <br>
    Look nice: Cleans up long, messy tracking links. <br>
    Track clicks: Shows how many people click your link. <br>
    Easy sharing: Simple to print on paper or put in a QR code.
  </p>

